          "id": "b-dasou1",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p><div><b><span class=\"big\">In Short</span></b></div><ul><li><b>What I Owned:</b> The entire second act's gameplay and puzzles, the camera and control feel, and the playtest process.</li><li><b>Hardest Problem:</b> A puzzle players couldn't see. Reframing the camera, sightlines and lighting raised the solve rate to about 90% from previous 70%.</li><li><b>What it Shows:</b> Designing for players who have never held a controller, teaching without text, and turning playtest observations into specific changes.</li></ul></p>"
        },
